        <type>Expected&lt; Image &gt;</type>
        <definition>Expected&lt; Image &gt; MR::convertRasterToImage</definition>
        <argsstring>(const Raster &amp;raster)</argsstring>
        <name>convertRasterToImage</name>
        <qualifiedname>MR::convertRasterToImage</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const Raster &amp;</type>
          <declname>raster</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>converts a raster with one layer to an image (the rows are reordered from bottom to top):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>the values of one channel are scaled from the range of finite values to gray colors, NaN and infinite values become black;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>three or more channels are RGB or RGBA colors (the channels after the fourth are ignored): integer values keep their high byte and are taken as unsigned ones, floating-point values are clamped to [0, 1], NaN becomes 0 </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
