        </param>
        <param>
          <type>size_t</type>
          <declname>size</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>converts the values of a raster to floats in dst, which has room for size = dims.x * dims.y * dims.z values, in the order of the raster:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>one channel is taken as is;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>three or more channels give the luma 0.299 R + 0.587 G + 0.114 B of the first three; fails for two channels, an unknown type, negative dimensions, data whose size does not match the dimensions, or another size </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
